findings.body:
`InsecureSkipVerify: true` is set on every client from `NewClient()`, with no staging/prod gate. Any network path that can MITM the ledger host can present an arbitrary certificate and the client will trust it, exposing ledger traffic to interception and modification.

The comment references staging and TICKET-77, but a comment is not a control — production builds get the same transport.

**Fix:** default to verification; only skip when an explicit non-prod config is set. Better: load the staging CA into `tls.Config.RootCAs` so verification stays on.

```go
Transport: &http.Transport{
    TLSClientConfig: &tls.Config{
        MinVersion: tls.VersionTLS12,
        // RootCAs: stagingPool, // trust staging CA
        // InsecureSkipVerify only if conf.AllowInsecureTLS && conf.Env != "production"
    },
},
```
